    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Safety\nIt you are sitting in an exit row\nand you cannot understand this\ncard or cannot see well enough\nto follow these instructions,\nplease tell a crew member.\nSicherheit\nSécurité\nSeguridad\nB-B7\nUNITED\nAIRLINES\n574 59\nWenn Sie neben einem Ausgang sitzen und Sie verstehen\nkein Englisch, bitte verständigen Sie die Flugzeugbesatzung.\nSi vous êtes assis dans une rangée de sièges à côté d'une\nsortie et ne comprenez pas la langue anglaise, veuillez\nle dire à un membre de l'équipage.\nSi usted se encuentra sentado en una corrida de asientos\npróxima a una salida y no entiende el idioma Inglés como\npara seguir estas instrucciones por favor avísele a una\nazatata.\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to ift, push,\npull, and maneuver when opening. Because of this, and\nfor the safety of all passengers, Federal Law requires\nthat we only seat qualified passengers next to exits.\nIf you are sitting in an exit row, you may be asked to\nopen the exit and assist our crew in the event of an\nemergency. Please ask to be reseated if you:\n•Have a physical condition which may not be visible and\nwhich may prevent you from helping\n•Think you lack the strength, mobility, dexterity, or\nbalance required to open the exit and assist our crew.\n•Do not think you could reach the exit, open it, and get\nout quickly.\n•Believe the physical exertion required to open the exit\nwould injure you.\n•Are hearing impaired and could not hear commands\nfrom our crew.\n•Are notable to give oral commands to others.\n•Do not understand the instructions in this brochure.\n•Have other responsibilities (such as a small child to\ncare for) which would prevent you from helping.\n•Are less than 15 years old.\n•Do not wish to help in this way.\nFederal regulations require all passengers,\nregardless of where they are sitting or their physical\ncondition, to review this card, for their safety.\nFollow these instructions, the directions of crew\nmembers, and placarded signs.\nWhen finished reviewing this card please return it\nto the seat pocket for our next customer.",
      "Flotation cushion\n#*#\nSchwimmfahige sitzkissen\nCoussins flotteurs\nAsiento flotante\nCA 344 2/92\nPrinted in the U.S.A.",
      "Take-off \u0026 landing\n81129\nStart und Landung\nDécollage et atterissage\nDespegar y aterrizar\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through a\nwindow to check outside\nfor the following:\nSmoke\nIf smoke is so thick you can not see out,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nFire\nIf there is fire outside the aircraft,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nDebris/\nObstructions\nIf there is metal debris or obstructions,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nNo smoking\nRauchen verboten\nDéfense de fumer\nNo fumar\nEmergency exits\nNotausgänge\nSorties de secours\nSalidas de emergencia\nA\nA\nExit\n3*0\nEXIT\nDirect passengers\naway from aircraft.\nAusgang\nSortie\nSalida\nB\n2\nOxygen\n1'1\nSauerstoff\nOxygène\nOxigeno\nCheck that the slide has properly\ninflated and is in good condition.\nUse handles to stabilize slide.\nCopyright © Aero Safety Graphics Inc. 1992. All rights reserved."
    ],
